.TH ZVM-DEDUPE 1 "October 2026" "ZVM" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-dedupe \- hard-link identical files across installed Zig versions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm dedupe
.RI [ version ...]
.br
.B zvm dedupe
.BR --auto " " on | off
.SH DESCRIPTION
Hash every regular file in the given installed versions (all of them when none
are given) with SHA-256 and replace duplicates with hard links into the
content-addressed store at
.IR ~/.zvm/store/ .
Patch releases of the same Zig series share almost every file except the
compiler binary, so this roughly halves the space two of them take; releases
further apart share less.
.PP
Files are only merged when their content, permission bits and (on Unix-like
systems) owner all match, because hard links share one inode. Symbolic links,
empty files and setuid/setgid/sticky files are left alone.
.PP
Each file is replaced by linking the store copy to a temporary name in the same
directory and renaming that over the original, so an interrupted run never
leaves a file missing. Running it again finishes the job and otherwise changes
nothing. Files that cannot be hard-linked (another filesystem, or one without
hard-link support) are left untouched and reported; they do not fail the run.
.PP
A deduped file is shared: editing it in place changes it in every version that
links to it. A later run detects store entries that no longer match their hash
and stops sharing them, but it cannot undo the edit; reinstall with
.B zvm install --force
instead.
.PP
Store files no installed version links to any more are removed by
.BR zvm-clean (1)
and after
.BR zvm-uninstall (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --auto " " on | off
Set whether
.BR zvm-install (1)
dedupes each newly installed version automatically, then exit.
Stored as
.B autoDedupe
in
.IR ~/.zvm/settings.json .
Off by default.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zvm dedupe
zvm dedupe 0.15.1 0.15.2
zvm dedupe --auto on
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zvm-clean (1),
.BR zvm-install (1),
.BR zvm-uninstall (1)
